# cw143, the storm walker (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 3: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw143
revision 3
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_quarry_mossfield
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the storm walker
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=nervy talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk sleeps_badly_before_storms
likes spiced_cider long_walks old_maps summer_evenings
dislikes cold_tea crowds
fears the_deep_wood_after_dusk thunder_over_an_open_orchard
hopes a_long_walk_with_clear_sky steady_work_for_the_household
topics work +0.4 weather +0.5 pastimes +0.3 family +0.3 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=blunt gossip=reluctant refuse=direct tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# checks the #sky# before bed, carries an old #map# on aimless #walks#, and avoids the deep #wood# at dusk.

words
oath! = Cloud and crooked road | By the sleepless sky
saying! = A storm keeps its own hour | Walk until the road explains itself
sky = sky | open sky
cloud = cloud | storm cloud
clouds = clouds | storm clouds
storm = storm | hard storm
storms = storms | hard storms
thunder = thunder | distant thunder
rain = rain | shower
wind = wind | lake wind
night = night | late hour
sleep = sleep | night's rest
bed = bed | own bed
roof = roof | cottage roof
window = window | small window
apple = apple | picked apple
apples = apples | orchard fruit
orchard = orchard | apple ground
tree = tree | apple tree
trees = trees | orchard trees
branch = branch | bough
row = row | planted row
rows = rows | planted rows
ladder = ladder | picking ladder
basket = basket | picking basket
crate = crate | fruit crate
crates = crates | fruit crates
tray = tray | drying tray
trays = trays | drying trays
store = store | drying house
market = market | market square
price = price | asking price
coin = coin | pay
bread = bread | loaf
tea = tea | cup of tea
cider = cider | spiced cider
spice = spice | warm spice
cup = cup | warm cup
walk = walk | long walk
walks = walks | long walks
map = map | old map
maps = maps | old maps
road = road | High Road
path = path | footpath
wood = wood | deep wood
shadow = shadow | dark patch
lake = lake | Glasswater
shore = shore | lakeshore
city = city | Ridgemere
crowd = crowd | press of people
home = home | shared cottage
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
gate = gate | cottage gate
evening = evening | summer dusk
soil = soil | wet earth
field = field | open field
weather = weather | changing sky
fire = fire | hearth fire

any
opinion @1 city against 2 : A #city# crowd gives me no room to turn around. | I know the #road# here better than any street there.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : Too much #cider# can turn a plain account into a foolish claim. | An approaching #storm# is easier to face sober.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : Their #store# has work and still leaves good #hands# outside. | I would rather rely on the #orchard# crew.
opinion @1 merchants against 3 : They raise the #bread# #price# without raising our pay. | I ask what they gave for the #apples# before I believe their hardship.
opinion @1 newcomers against 2 : A new face near our #crates# gets my attention. | I need to see someone work before I trust them with a #ladder#.
opinion @1 road against 1 : I will walk a familiar #path#, but the long #road# has too many surprises. | The turn by the #wood# is especially poor after dusk.
opinion @1 strangers against 1 : I keep a stranger at the #gate# until I know what follows them. | They can ask directions without entering the #home#.
opinion @1 times against 1 : The #market# takes more #coin# from every #crate#. | A day's work should buy more than yesterday's #bread#.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. Give me the reason for this visit. | #greet#. The #sky# looks wrong for a long talk.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : I am carrying #crates#; speak as we move. | Give me until this #tray# is set down.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I have #cider# warming. | You can join my #walk# after the #store# closes.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : I did not #sleep# much with that #cloud# coming. | #greet#. The #rows# are still wet.
line @1 greet.return : #welcome_back#. The #sky# has not cleared. | You have caught me between #crates#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Leave the #rain# at the door and sit. | There is #bread# and a dry chair.
line @1 again.open : We were talking about the #map# before the #wind# rose. | Did the #road# change your mind?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Stay out of the #wood# after dark. | #saying.capitalize#. The #roof# wants one more look.
line @1 farewell.return : The #cider# may be ready next time. | Perhaps we can walk in clear weather.
line @1 react.news : Give me the facts in their order. | Let me rest the #basket# before you go on.
line @1 react.news.new : That has not reached our #store#. | Which traveller brought the word here?
line @1 react.news.known : Someone at the #market# told me an earlier part. | Yours is a clearer account.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #hedge#, I want a witness, not a #crowd# repeating it. | A bad #map# can make a straight #road# look bent.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That is cruel news. I can leave the #crates# for now. | Sit near the #fire# where the #wind# cannot reach.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. I hope the #home# is celebrating. | That is a reason to open the #cider#.
line @1 answer.how : I was awake through the #night#, but I am standing. | A clear #sky# would settle me more.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : A full #row# still needs picking. | The #trays# are waiting for the last #crate#.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #storm# wake you? | Did you find time for a hot drink?
line @1 sympathise : I can walk with you while you talk. | I will not dress it up with a saying.
line @1 reassure : A #storm# passes, even when it takes its time. | We can find the #path# again in daylight.
line @1 decline : No. I will not take the #road# by the #wood#. | The #store# needs me for this #crate#.
line @1 accept_decline : Your answer is enough. | I shall not press you.
line @1 thank : You brought the #trays# under the #roof# before #rain#. | I noticed you stayed to finish the #row#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : The #basket# was within reach. | I knew that turn on the #path#.
line @1 preclose : The #clouds# tell me to cover the #crates#. | I have a #roof# to inspect before bed.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #map# has more confidence than sense. | I would trust your #tea# to go cold before a kettle.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will check the #window#. | #bc_fair_enough#. The #crate# stays.
line @1 give.advice : Cover the #crates# before a #storm# reaches the #orchard#. | Follow the open #path# when the #wood# grows dim.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep off the lonely #road# tonight. | Walk with someone you know if you must go.
scene storm_sleep
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I sleep badly when a #storm# is coming, even before the #clouds# show. | The #roof# seems to make a different sound at #night#.
b : How can you tell? | Do you rise early?
a : I wake and listen. | Often before dawn.

scene window_cloud
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : From the #window# I watch #clouds# cross the #lake#. | Once they reach the #wood#, I cover the #crates#.
b : Is that enough warning? | Do you watch all night?
a : Usually. | When the #wind# will not settle.

scene thunder_roof
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #thunder.capitalize# over a sound #roof# is easier than waiting for it outside. | I count the time between a flash and the next rumble.
b : Does that calm you? | Would you check the #orchard# in it?
a : It gives my mind a task. | Only if a #crate# was left out.

scene long_walk
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I take a #walk# without deciding where it ends. | The #road# is better when I owe it no destination.
b : Do you carry a map? | How far do you go?
a : An old one, for the mistakes. | Until the #lake# comes back into view.

scene crooked_map
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My oldest #map# bends the #road# toward a hill that has never moved. | I keep it because someone walked there and remembered it badly.
b : Do you correct it? | Does it mislead you?
a : In the margin. | Only when I forget to look up.

scene wood_edge
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #path# beside the #wood# shortens a walk, but I avoid it near dusk. | The #shadow# there grows before the rest of the world darkens.
b : Why avoid it? | Would you go with someone?
a : I do not like how quiet it becomes. | In full light.

scene summer_evening
when topic=weather here.season=summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : After the #store# shuts on a summer #evening#, I can keep walking. | The #lake# keeps the last light longer than the #wood#.
b : Can the walk ease your rest? | Do you walk alone?
a : More than cold #tea# does. | Often.

scene spiced_cider
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Warm #cider# with #spice# can settle me after a rough #night#. | I pour a #cup# before the #storm# reaches the #roof#.
b : Do you drink much? | Does it help?
a : One #cup#. | Enough to stop pacing.

scene cold_tea
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #tea.capitalize# left cold by the #trays# is barely worth a #cup#. | I will drink it rather than waste it.
b : Do you prefer cider? | Why leave it so long?
a : When there is #spice#. | The #crates# needed me.

scene apple_row
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I pick one #row# at a time so no #tree# is missed. | A hurried worker leaves sound #apples# on the shaded side.
b : Do you go back? | Does it slow you?
a : Before the #ladder# moves. | Less than a missed #crate#.

scene ladder_check
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I test the #ladder# foot before carrying a #basket# up. | Wet #soil# can move under a rung.
b : Has it slipped? | Who steadies it?
a : Once. | Another picker when available.

scene drying_tray
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I bring the #trays# inside before the air turns damp. | A #crate# left open during #rain# can lose a day's care.
b : Does the fruit spoil? | Can you save it?
a : Some of it. | By drying it at once.

scene market_crowd
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #crowd# at the #market# makes it hard to hear the #price#. | I ask a seller to name the sum once more.
b : Do they dislike that? | Do you bargain?
a : Some do. | When the #coin# is thin.

scene city_smoke
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I found the #city# loud enough to make me miss the #wind#. | The #road# home was a relief after its crowded streets.
b : Will you return? | Was it all bad?
a : If work demands it. | I met one kind person.

scene spouse_roof
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #self.spouse# can tell when I have spent a #night# listening for #thunder#. | We check the #roof# together in daylight.
b : Does your spouse sleep through it? | Do you repair it?
a : Better than I do. | Small leaks, yes.

scene shared_home
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #home# holds many working #hands# and little quiet. | A long #walk# gives me room to think before supper.
b : Do you mind the company? | Do you tell them where you go?
a : I value it. | I leave word.

scene approaching_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# on the #orchard# means we cover the #crates# first. | I do not wait for the #trays# to feel damp.
b : Can you finish picking? | Do you hurry?
a : If the shower is light. | I move steadily.

story night_before_storm [topic=weather self.age>=25]
  : I lay awake while the #sky# still showed stars.
  : By morning a #storm# had crossed the #lake# and soaked the last #crate#.
  b : You sensed it before the clouds. Could you save the fruit?
  : Most of it, after we spread it on #trays#.

story map_walk [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : I carried an old #map# on a #walk# with no errand.
  : Its #road# ended at a #field#, so I followed the #shore# instead.
  b : A better route than the map. Did you get lost?
  : Only in thought; I knew the way #home#.

story wood_turn [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I reached the #wood# #path# as the #shadow# lengthened.
  : I turned for the open #road#, though it made the journey longer.
  b : You chose the way you could see. Did something follow you?
  : Nothing I saw. The quiet was enough.

rule @bark_cloud
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The #clouds# are crossing the #lake#. | I should look at the #roof#.

rule @bark_crates
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Cover this #crate# before #rain#. | One more #tray# belongs inside.

rule @bark_map
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say That #map# has a road in the wrong place. | A #walk# might settle me.

rule @bark_night
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 11h
say I will check the #window# once more. | The #wind# has changed.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. State your business before the #rain# starts. | #greet#. I am moving these #crates# inside.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You know I watch the #sky#; it looks unsettled. | Back again? The #map# is still by the door.
dlg @1 resident.job : I pick #apples# for #self.workplace# and bring them to the #trays#. | My work runs from the #rows# to the covered #crates#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Take the open #road#. | #saying.capitalize#. The #crates# need covering.
graft resident.hub
choice Why watch the sky so closely? -> sky
node sky
say I sleep poorly before #storms#. If I see the #clouds# early, I can at least cover the #crates#.
free
choice Where do your walks go? -> walks
choice Back to the orchard. -> hub
node walks
say Wherever the #road# stays open. I carry an old #map# and let the #lake# guide me back.
choice Back to the orchard. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
